Ladybird’s table fixup now generates an anonymous inline-table only when
the parent of the misparented cells is an inline box (display: inline),
and a block-level table otherwise, such as inside an inline-block.
Chrome 158, Firefox 151 and WebKit 26.5 give a 300px cell on two lines
in all eight cases of the new test, run with engine-compare, including
an inline flow-root, an inline-block with inline content before the
cell, and a span inside a 300px block.

Blink’s LayoutTable::CreateAnonymousWithParent() uses kInlineTable only
when the parent IsLayoutInline(), and in WebKit, RenderTreeBuilder::
Table::createAnonymousTableWithStyle() uses InlineTable only when the
parent’s display is InlineFlow. Gecko’s nsCSSFrameConstructor turns its
MozTable pseudo into MozInlineTable only for a parent whose display
IsInlineFlow(), or a ruby base or text. This paragraph comes from
reading their sources, not running them.
